$Energy radiated, \mathrm{U} \propto \mathrm{AT}^{4} \mathrm{t}\begin{array}{l}
\Rightarrow \frac{\mathrm{U}_{2}}{\mathrm{U}_{1}}=\frac{\mathrm{A} / 2(2 \mathrm{ T})^{4} \cdot \mathrm{t}}{\mathrm{AT}^{4} \cdot \mathrm{t}}=8 \\
\Rightarrow \mathrm{U}_{2}=8 \mathrm{U}_{1} \\
\Rightarrow \mathrm{mS} \Delta \mathrm{t}_{2}=8 \mathrm{mS} \Delta \mathrm{t}_{1} \\
\Rightarrow \Delta \mathrm{t}_{2}=8 \Delta \mathrm{t}_{1}
\end{array}$
